WEBVTT

00:02.750 --> 00:05.230
<i>I worked as a salaryman 
for a toxic company,</i>

00:05.230 --> 00:06.960
<i>until I reincarnated...</i>

00:06.960 --> 00:11.110
<i>in a crazy world where everything is 
dropped by monsters in dungeons.</i>

00:11.110 --> 00:15.870
<i>In my new life, I'm level 1, 
but I have a unique skill</i>

00:15.870 --> 00:17.920
<i>that puts all of my drop rates at rank S.</i>

00:18.340 --> 00:19.780
<i>And today I'm...</i>

00:20.260 --> 00:23.960
<i>swimming in rare drops during 
a battle for a new dungeon!</i>

00:23.960 --> 00:28.690
<i>But for some reason, I'm just 
not okay with this drop!</i>

00:36.140 --> 00:45.270
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

02:00.010 --> 02:05.020
<b>This Dungeon Battle Is a Vortex of Schemes</b>

02:05.020 --> 02:07.290
I have to burn the trash right away.

02:15.420 --> 02:16.620
Are you okay?!

02:18.480 --> 02:21.060
I'm fine.

02:21.730 --> 02:24.350
You can't use any more magic.

02:24.350 --> 02:25.900
You need to rest.

02:27.220 --> 02:30.840
They're... depending on me to do this.

02:31.250 --> 02:33.940
So... I have to...

02:36.230 --> 02:38.090
I've seen it all too often.

02:38.090 --> 02:41.840
People get so overwhelmed by 
responsibility that their health crashes,

02:41.840 --> 02:43.480
their spirits are crushed...

02:44.410 --> 02:46.110
Some people even die.

02:46.110 --> 02:49.400
But... this is all I can do.

02:51.110 --> 02:53.580
Sorry to make this about me,

02:53.580 --> 02:56.010
but I don't want to see that happen again.

03:05.160 --> 03:07.090
Yoda, what was that?

03:07.320 --> 03:10.640
When two healing bullets fuse, 
they become a sleep bullet.

03:11.740 --> 03:13.710
I'm making her get some good sleep.

03:13.710 --> 03:15.420
That's for the best.

03:29.120 --> 03:30.500
It's already so late?!

03:39.010 --> 03:40.160
I'm too late!

03:53.860 --> 03:55.000
Wow...

04:00.380 --> 04:02.400
Sorry to keep you waiting!

04:02.400 --> 04:05.370
Please bring all the trash over here!

04:06.300 --> 04:08.730
What a great haul of homing bullets!

04:10.640 --> 04:12.830
Line up, please!

04:12.830 --> 04:14.990
Oh! Miss!

04:15.810 --> 04:18.100
You should get some more sleep.

04:18.100 --> 04:20.980
She's right. Let us handle things here...

04:20.980 --> 04:23.660
Oh, did you wake up because you're hungry?

04:23.660 --> 04:24.590
Huh?

04:25.490 --> 04:26.470
What?!

04:28.740 --> 04:30.900
Don't worry about the trash.

04:30.900 --> 04:34.110
We moved this tent closer 
to the collection site.

04:34.110 --> 04:36.420
Eat up before it gets cold!

04:49.210 --> 04:50.670
Delicious.

04:52.600 --> 04:54.630
You cry when you eat something delicious?

04:54.630 --> 04:56.680
Just like Yoda!

04:57.100 --> 05:00.800
You're just like him in the way 
you push yourself too hard, too.

05:01.200 --> 05:02.290
Really?

05:02.290 --> 05:04.220
I can tell.

05:08.850 --> 05:11.910
We haven't asked your name yet.

05:12.330 --> 05:14.320
My name is Celeste.

05:16.180 --> 05:17.710
I see.

05:17.710 --> 05:21.630
So the dungeon drops are tax-exempt 
until its ownership is decided.

05:21.630 --> 05:25.540
That's why so many adventurers are 
here even at this time of year.

05:25.540 --> 05:29.370
Yes, and they produce more 
and more trash every day.

05:29.730 --> 05:32.230
That's way more than one person can handle.

05:32.230 --> 05:35.150
We'll help you out when we have time.

05:36.940 --> 05:38.860
Thank you so much!

05:40.980 --> 05:44.580
This is the only work I can do...

05:45.740 --> 05:47.500
There's nothing else?

05:54.090 --> 05:55.960
She fell asleep.

05:55.960 --> 06:00.390
She finally gets to share a little of 
the burden she's been carrying alone.

06:00.890 --> 06:03.500
And the relief was so great, she fell asleep.

06:08.080 --> 06:10.730
That's way more powerful 
than it was yesterday!

06:10.730 --> 06:13.280
Her color is much better now, as well.

06:13.280 --> 06:15.520
She looks much prettier today.

06:15.520 --> 06:16.940
You're right.

06:21.140 --> 06:23.330
Since you gave me a chance to rest,

06:23.330 --> 06:26.160
my magic recovered to an
 even greater level than normal.

06:26.160 --> 06:29.830
But you'll go back to the way you 
were if you overwork yourself again.

06:29.830 --> 06:31.770
We have food and a bed.

06:31.770 --> 06:34.820
Please stay in our tent 
until this event is over.

06:36.870 --> 06:40.180
But... I couldn't possibly ask more of you.

06:41.750 --> 06:46.000
That tent is far too 
comfortable, so if I stay...

06:46.000 --> 06:48.840
That's thanks to Emily's unique skill.

06:48.840 --> 06:50.580
You can't escape it!

06:52.200 --> 06:54.530
What an incredible skill...

07:00.210 --> 07:02.340
I will stay with you for a while, then.

07:02.600 --> 07:03.790
That settles it.

07:04.770 --> 07:08.640
I'm going to go say hello at the Secro HQ.

07:08.640 --> 07:10.930
I'll go with you as far as the shops.

07:10.930 --> 07:14.780
We'll be back by lunchtime. 
You can head back to the tent.

07:20.870 --> 07:25.430
Now that I look at it again, 
this place really is its own little town.

07:30.040 --> 07:31.960
Why are you selling these here?

07:31.960 --> 07:34.200
You'd be surprised how well they sell.

07:34.200 --> 07:37.900
Lots of men who've come here to work 
buy them as gifts for their wives.

07:40.500 --> 07:42.980
The most expensive one is a million pilos?!

07:42.980 --> 07:44.690
I definitely couldn't afford that.

07:44.980 --> 07:47.060
They're so beautiful!

07:47.380 --> 07:49.470
You like this sort of thing, Emily?

07:49.730 --> 07:51.830
I think rings are just lovely.

07:52.250 --> 07:54.350
They're too expensive for me to buy, though.

07:54.350 --> 07:57.480
But rings are just... special, you know?

07:59.890 --> 08:01.870
Thank you for coming here, Mr. Sato.

08:02.170 --> 08:04.300
I'm Duke, the man in charge here.

08:04.300 --> 08:05.530
It's a pleasure to meet you.

08:05.530 --> 08:06.740
Same to you.

08:07.100 --> 08:09.080
Now, take a look at this.

08:09.090 --> 08:14.890
<b>Level 1

\hMonster: Rainbow Slime
\hDrop: Soybeans</b>

08:09.090 --> 08:14.890
<b>Level 2

Monster: Treant
Drop: Chicken Breast</b>

08:09.090 --> 08:14.890
<b>\h\h\h\hLevel 3

Monster: Killer Butterfly
Drop: Cabbage</b>

08:09.090 --> 08:14.890
<b>Level 4

Monster: Mandrake
Drop: Sliced Pork</b>

08:09.090 --> 08:14.890
<b>Level 5

\hMonster:
\hDanger Bear
\hDrop: Okra</b>

08:09.090 --> 08:14.890
<b>Level 6

\hMonster: Gray Slime
\hDrop: Beef Rib</b>

08:09.090 --> 08:14.890
<b>Level 7

Monster:
Mad Golem
Drop: Daikon Radish</b>

08:09.090 --> 08:14.890
<b>Level 8

Monster:
Sandworm
Drop: Round Steak</b>

08:09.800 --> 08:14.550
It's a sketch of Selen, the new dungeon 
Secro and Hetero are fighting over.

08:14.890 --> 08:16.920
So it has ten floors...

08:17.190 --> 08:19.320
We already know what drops are found there.

08:19.320 --> 08:22.550
Vegetables on odd-numbered floors, 
and meats on even-numbered floors.

08:22.550 --> 08:24.010
An even split?

08:24.010 --> 08:26.870
Yes, so we can't decide based on that.

08:26.870 --> 08:29.810
That's why we decided that 
the side whose floors

08:29.810 --> 08:32.800
yield the most rare drops 
within the time limit wins.

08:32.800 --> 08:35.090
Got it. I'll go right in and—

08:35.090 --> 08:36.250
You don't need to go hunting.

08:36.250 --> 08:39.710
Adventurers who find rare monsters 
on the vegetable floors

08:39.710 --> 08:41.910
will capture them alive and wait for you.

08:41.910 --> 08:43.000
Huh?

08:43.000 --> 08:44.990
It's the most efficient way.

08:44.990 --> 08:48.520
We've solicited help with 
the promise of reward money.

08:48.520 --> 08:51.430
We just need you to focus 
on getting us rare drops.

08:51.710 --> 08:55.280
<i>They built up this whole plan around me?</i>

08:55.280 --> 08:57.520
<i>That never would've 
happened in my old world,</i>

08:57.520 --> 09:00.260
<i>but this really seems worth doing.</i>

09:00.260 --> 09:01.470
They've got a rare one!

09:02.200 --> 09:03.680
On the first level!

09:07.680 --> 09:11.310
As long as it's in our custody, 
we have the option to kill it.

09:11.310 --> 09:13.000
Take all the time you need.

09:13.000 --> 09:13.900
Got it.

09:18.500 --> 09:20.050
Who are they?

09:20.050 --> 09:22.150
The older man is Harvard.

09:22.490 --> 09:26.500
He holds the same role in Hetero's 
Dungeon Association that I do in Secro.

09:27.270 --> 09:29.280
Next to him is Eugene, an adventurer.

09:29.280 --> 09:32.650
He's renowned for his skills, 
but his plant drop rate is at rank F.

09:33.620 --> 09:36.190
Why bring an adventurer 
with F-ranked drop rates?

09:36.190 --> 09:40.400
He'll defeat rare plant monsters, 
and they probably won't drop anything.

09:40.820 --> 09:44.610
That'll leave fewer chances 
for us to find rare drops.

09:45.050 --> 09:47.560
So he's here to sabotage us?

09:47.560 --> 09:51.690
Exactly. But we've already got 
the initiative this time.

09:55.560 --> 09:57.280
Hold it still.

09:58.160 --> 09:59.890
Hurry up, would you?!

10:03.400 --> 10:04.980
There! Now it's—

10:08.940 --> 10:10.540
What's happening?!

10:10.540 --> 10:15.930
<i>That one won't die unless you destroy 
the core hidden somewhere in its body.</i>

10:15.930 --> 10:19.900
<i>Attack it anywhere else, 
and it'll bounce back even stronger.</i>

10:20.330 --> 10:23.600
<i>I know exactly where its core is.</i>

10:29.010 --> 10:32.430
Now it's first come, first serve!
Go, Eugene!

10:42.360 --> 10:43.530
You're mine!

10:53.780 --> 10:55.880
You can see its core, too?!

10:55.880 --> 10:58.000
Yeah, something like that.

11:01.350 --> 11:04.630
The rare drop, soybean sprouts, is ours!

11:04.630 --> 11:06.550
That gives us a head start!

11:06.550 --> 11:07.760
Damn!

11:11.560 --> 11:13.110
Here's your reward.

11:13.110 --> 11:14.730
Put it somewhere safe.

11:14.730 --> 11:16.750
You're giving me this much?

11:16.750 --> 11:19.510
It's an appropriate amount, 
given your contribution.

11:19.510 --> 11:22.510
The soybean sprouts we 
got are yours, as well.

11:22.510 --> 11:24.650
You can exchange them for money 
at the trade post we set up.

11:27.990 --> 11:30.620
This is incidental income 
I wasn't expecting.

11:30.620 --> 11:34.190
Maybe now, if I can do that one more time...

11:35.040 --> 11:40.050
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

11:35.040 --> 11:40.050
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

11:35.520 --> 11:37.640
Where did Emily go?

11:37.640 --> 11:39.280
Here I am!

11:40.050 --> 11:45.050
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

11:40.050 --> 11:45.050
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

11:41.680 --> 11:45.040
I can't see the director's face anymore!

11:45.730 --> 11:47.110
I'm back.

11:47.110 --> 11:48.540
Welcome back.

11:48.870 --> 11:51.140
You've had a very long day.

11:51.140 --> 11:54.470
Was the dungeon-conquering job difficult?

11:54.470 --> 11:58.650
Yeah. Hetero's using an adventurer 
with F-ranked vegetable drop rates

11:58.650 --> 12:00.820
to kill our chances at rare drops.

12:00.820 --> 12:03.830
Wow, that's how they've chosen to fight?

12:03.830 --> 12:06.340
But I actually finished that early.

12:06.340 --> 12:09.250
I'm late because I made 
a stop on the way back.

12:12.140 --> 12:16.000
Oh! You bought the ring we saw this morning?

12:16.000 --> 12:18.270
It really is beautiful!

12:18.900 --> 12:19.830
Emily...

12:19.830 --> 12:20.940
Huh?

12:20.940 --> 12:22.860
Would you accept this?

12:22.860 --> 12:25.670
Wha... What?!

12:25.670 --> 12:28.350
I mean, you help me out all the time.

12:28.350 --> 12:30.340
But it's too expensive...

12:30.340 --> 12:33.100
I got incidental bonus pay. And...

12:33.350 --> 12:36.230
I was able to make good 
money on the first level.

12:37.030 --> 12:41.400
When you said rings are special, 
I started to think...

12:41.400 --> 12:44.830
What's special to me is that I met you.

12:45.150 --> 12:47.230
That's why I want to give you this.

12:51.310 --> 12:53.970
Thanks for everything, Emily.

12:56.370 --> 13:00.690
No present has ever made me this happy.

13:02.280 --> 13:04.080
Thank you.

13:07.930 --> 13:15.730
"Emily"

Level   22/40

Drop Status

<b>Plants D (+1) 
Animals E (+1) 
Minerals E (+1) 
Magic E (+1) 
Specials E (+1)</b>

13:07.940 --> 13:10.500
They all have "+1" next to them!

13:10.500 --> 13:12.520
I've never seen this before!

13:12.520 --> 13:14.900
Is it because of your power?

13:15.720 --> 13:18.470
Uh, actually...

13:18.470 --> 13:21.370
The guy told me he had more 
of the same ring in stock,

13:21.370 --> 13:26.380
and I was really curious as to 
what kind of stray would emerge

13:26.380 --> 13:28.290
from a million-pilo ring, so...

13:30.260 --> 13:32.550
It's pretty easy to make a profit here,

13:32.550 --> 13:34.870
so I tried it, figuring I'd just 
buy another if it didn't work.

13:39.780 --> 13:42.620
And I ended up getting back 
the same kind of ring,

13:42.620 --> 13:44.490
but with an effect attached.

13:45.680 --> 13:47.620
That's so like you, Yoda.

13:48.340 --> 13:50.180
Let's go test it out.

13:50.180 --> 13:51.160
Right!

13:52.770 --> 13:56.190
<b>Selen Level 2</b>

13:53.940 --> 13:55.330
This level's okay?

13:55.330 --> 13:56.180
Yes.

13:57.550 --> 13:59.910
Oh, there's one! A treant!

14:09.280 --> 14:11.320
Ooh, a chicken breast?

14:11.320 --> 14:13.030
I really got a drop!

14:15.010 --> 14:16.780
You're that happy about it?

14:16.780 --> 14:20.790
I've always wanted to get a 
meat drop, even if only once!

14:21.160 --> 14:23.030
This is my first one ever!

14:24.590 --> 14:27.710
My animal drop rate was at rank F.

14:27.710 --> 14:32.710
F is just one rank below E, 
but there's actually a huge difference.

14:32.710 --> 14:36.500
People whose drop rates are 
all F are known as "F Final,"

14:36.500 --> 14:38.980
and some dungeons don't 
even permit them entry.

14:38.980 --> 14:40.560
Really?

14:44.600 --> 14:47.810
Go get Harvard! He should be nearby!

14:47.810 --> 14:50.900
Is that this floor's rare monster?!

14:53.560 --> 14:54.320
Emily!

14:54.320 --> 14:55.720
I'm okay!

14:56.940 --> 14:58.300
You—

14:58.300 --> 14:59.300
Good!

14:59.980 --> 15:01.580
Go on, shoot.

15:01.840 --> 15:05.160
You seem to have very good drop rates.

15:05.160 --> 15:08.000
Please go ahead and kill this treant beard.

15:09.170 --> 15:12.020
<i>If I kill it, it'll definitely
 drop something,</i>

15:12.020 --> 15:15.180
<i>and that'll bring Hetero's 
score even with Secro's.</i>

15:17.820 --> 15:20.350
What's wrong? Aren't you going to kill it?

15:20.350 --> 15:23.170
None of us would mind if you did,

15:23.170 --> 15:25.850
as long as the spoils drop on this floor.

15:28.470 --> 15:32.190
<i>I can tell just from looking at him 
that his animal drop rate is high.</i>

15:35.230 --> 15:37.450
Damn it! What do I do?

15:39.380 --> 15:40.760
Yoda!

15:45.040 --> 15:46.410
<i>Of course!</i>

16:11.750 --> 16:13.520
Thanks, Emily.

16:18.590 --> 16:21.860
I remembered what you said last night.

16:21.860 --> 16:25.760
Without this ring, my animal drop rate is F.

16:25.760 --> 16:27.990
Very smart of you to come up
 with that on the spot!

16:28.500 --> 16:30.810
I'm glad I could be of use.

16:30.810 --> 16:34.000
All that time thinking about 
how I could help was worth it.

16:36.420 --> 16:37.710
Mr. Sato.

16:38.060 --> 16:41.070
I hear you did some quick thinking 
for us on the second level.

16:41.070 --> 16:42.060
Thank you.

16:42.060 --> 16:44.440
It wasn't me. It was my partner.

16:44.440 --> 16:47.730
This adventurer has just earned 
some reward money, then.

16:47.730 --> 16:50.590
We do have a bit of a problem now, though.

16:52.360 --> 16:56.240
Hetero's backup adventurers 
will be here by tonight.

16:56.240 --> 16:58.920
That will triple their numbers.

16:59.280 --> 17:02.040
So they'll fill up the 
floors that drop meat?

17:02.040 --> 17:03.170
The reverse.

17:03.170 --> 17:05.920
They plan to fill up the odd-numbered floors,

17:05.920 --> 17:08.820
the ones with vegetables, 
with F-ranked adventurers.

17:08.820 --> 17:10.300
But that's...

17:12.960 --> 17:15.680
I guess our only choice is 
to fight fire with fire.

17:16.880 --> 17:19.510
No, let's finish this before 
the end of the day.

17:20.710 --> 17:23.390
If we get rare drops on 
floors 3, 5, 7, and 9,

17:23.390 --> 17:26.970
we'll be tied with them 
at the very least, right?

17:26.970 --> 17:29.720
If we could do that, 
we'd effectively win, but...

17:29.720 --> 17:34.410
Raise the reward for finding rare 
monsters all the way to ten million.

17:34.410 --> 17:36.190
What?! That's too much!

17:36.190 --> 17:40.110
If we pay that much and then don't get 
a rare drop, it'll be a huge loss!

17:40.110 --> 17:42.490
I have a 100% chance of 
getting that rare drop.

17:42.490 --> 17:43.830
Still...

17:43.830 --> 17:46.270
If I kill it and nothing drops,

17:46.270 --> 17:48.090
I'll pay you the same amount back.

17:54.970 --> 17:55.840
All right.

17:57.430 --> 18:01.130
I can't believe we've 
actually come this far!

18:01.260 --> 18:08.060
<b>Selen Level 3</b>

18:01.360 --> 18:06.120
The rare form of level 3's monster, 
the killer butterfly, is the evil butterfly.

18:06.120 --> 18:08.050
It drops Brussels sprouts.

18:08.190 --> 18:14.230
<b>Selen Level 5</b>

18:08.310 --> 18:12.370
The rare form of level 5's 
danger bear is the danger panda.

18:12.370 --> 18:14.240
It drops saltwort.

18:14.360 --> 18:20.660
<b>Selen Level 7</b>

18:14.650 --> 18:18.610
The rare form of level 7's 
mad golem is the rock golem.

18:18.600 --> 18:20.650
It drops daikon radish sprouts.

18:21.020 --> 18:24.640
It kinda sucks that all these 
"rare drops" are so basic,

18:24.640 --> 18:27.080
but in any case, once I kill 
this thing, we're done!

18:27.980 --> 18:29.930
One of its heads is its weakness,

18:29.930 --> 18:32.420
but every time it regenerates a head,
 its weakness changes!

18:32.800 --> 18:35.550
It's a royal pain to fight 
this thing legit, but...

18:51.100 --> 18:52.850
Enoki mushrooms...

18:54.140 --> 18:56.300
The last one's as lame as the rest.

18:56.300 --> 18:57.570
You did it!

18:57.570 --> 18:59.970
There's no way we can lose now!

18:59.970 --> 19:02.360
In fact, we might as well say we've won!

19:02.360 --> 19:04.110
All thanks to you, Duke.

19:04.110 --> 19:05.850
No need to be modest!

19:05.850 --> 19:09.190
I'll go report your achievement 
to HQ right now.

19:13.250 --> 19:14.750
<i>I'm not being modest.</i>

19:15.260 --> 19:18.810
<i>At my old office, every suggestion 
I offered was rejected.</i>

19:18.810 --> 19:24.180
<i>But you were on board with my idea to 
devote a budget of forty million to this.</i>

19:25.100 --> 19:26.390
<b>Selen Level 1</b>

19:26.380 --> 19:28.070
Whether we win or not,

19:28.070 --> 19:31.430
I just made a big purchase, so I'd 
like to make a little more money.

19:43.150 --> 19:44.570
What do you want?

19:45.100 --> 19:47.730
You've gone too far.

19:48.000 --> 19:51.200
All of these guys, and my self, 
have F Final drop rates.

19:51.200 --> 19:54.950
If we could have stopped Secro, 
the money would've been ours.

19:54.950 --> 19:57.260
But thanks to you, we're no longer needed.

20:03.920 --> 20:07.030
This magic circle has the same 
effect as a magic storm.

20:07.030 --> 20:09.480
You can no longer use your projectiles.

20:10.440 --> 20:12.360
I won't take your life...

20:13.020 --> 20:17.420
But I won't rest until I make sure 
you can no longer do your job!

20:22.650 --> 20:25.860
So long as I don't worry 
about being efficient...

20:28.880 --> 20:31.670
I'm stronger when I don't use my guns.

20:37.190 --> 20:38.570
If you can use them, go ahead—

20:40.050 --> 20:42.550
You <i>can</i> use them?!

20:43.150 --> 20:46.140
I've used them during a magic storm before.

20:52.700 --> 20:53.430
Huh?

20:59.950 --> 21:01.810
The pain is gone...

21:03.810 --> 21:06.390
This one's loaded with special bullets.

21:06.390 --> 21:08.420
It works just like healing magic.

21:13.520 --> 21:14.710
You...

21:14.710 --> 21:16.980
You probably won't believe me,

21:17.700 --> 21:20.260
but I understand how you guys feel.

21:20.260 --> 21:24.250
So if you can't rest otherwise, 
attack me all you want.

21:24.790 --> 21:27.870
If you get hurt doing it, 
I'll fix you up each time.

21:28.890 --> 21:30.940
But I won't lose, either.

21:31.270 --> 21:34.610
Because I have someone waiting 
for me to come home safe.

21:35.460 --> 21:36.770
I get it.

21:37.100 --> 21:40.470
I envy you for having someone like that.

21:40.470 --> 21:42.680
I didn't always have her.

21:42.680 --> 21:45.290
You might find someone of your own someday.

21:50.440 --> 21:51.710
I'm back.

21:51.710 --> 21:53.090
Welcome back!

21:53.090 --> 21:54.980
Oh, welcome back.

21:55.250 --> 21:56.760
We've been waiting for you!

21:56.760 --> 21:58.620
Dinner is already on the table.

21:59.330 --> 22:02.440
I've come... home.

22:04.690 --> 22:07.050
We... can see that.
